`bin/check-done fct_activity_daily` prints **DONE**.

## Summary

`fct_activity_daily` was skill-compliant structurally (grain comment, dedup on `event_id`/`ingested_at`, CTE style, `unique`+`not_null` on the primary key, YAML docs, `fct_` prefix, no PII columns), but `bin/data-diff` caught a real data bug: it cast `event_ts` to a date using the session's local time zone instead of UTC, so some events landed on the wrong day (visible as a phantom `2026-09-30` row and systematic under/over-counts for every other day).

**Fix:** changed the `activity_date` calculation to explicitly convert to UTC before casting to date:

```sql
-- event_ts is stored in UTC; the session time zone is not — say UTC explicitly.
cast(timezone('UTC', event_ts) as date) as activity_date,
```

This matches the "all timestamps are stored in UTC" convention and the explicit-UTC pattern already used in `bin/data-diff`'s source query.

### Commands run
```
DBT_PROFILES_DIR=. dbt build -s fct_activity_daily
bin/data-diff fct_activity_daily      # failed before the fix, passed after
bin/check-done fct_activity_daily     # -> DONE
```

All three data-diff checks (completeness, keys, nulls) now pass within tolerance, the SQL in `EVIDENCE.md` matches what the model actually produces, and all four planned `unique`/`not_null` tests ran and passed in the last `dbt build`. No prod runs were made at any point.
